# Line endings and binary files.
#
# Why this file exists: the repository is developed on Windows, where git defaults
# to core.autocrlf=true. Without a declaration here, a fresh checkout (or a
# `git archive` export) hands CRLF files to whoever reads them, and the contour
# test harnesses slice declarations out of client.js BY LINE — they then silently
# miss declarations and fail for a reason that has nothing to do with the engine.
# This actually happened with the first packaged archive.
#
# So: store and check out LF everywhere, and make the webp screenshots explicitly
# binary so nothing ever tries to normalise them.
* text=auto eol=lf

*.webp binary
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.ico binary
